        "note": "Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization (Liu, Tang, Zhang; public since July 2026) of the square-energy strengthening of Turán's theorem sqrt(s^+(G)), sqrt(s^-(G)) <= (1 - 1/omega(G)) n. It contains a doubly-nonnegative Motzkin–Straus inequality (SqOmega/DNN/MotzkinStraus.lean, dnnMotzkinStraus_*) proved via the Caro–Wei random partition, with vertex-count normalization. Code reuse: BN/Basic/Graph.lean (turanFactor and the elementary clique-number lemmas one_le_cliqueNum, two_le_cliqueNum_of_adj, cliqueNum_eq_one_iff_eq_bot, turanFactor_nonneg, turanFactor_pos) is copied from SqOmega/Graph.lean with a namespace change. The rest of the development is independent of SqOmega: Motzkin–Straus is used here in completely positive form with nonnegative edge weights (BN/MS/), which is what the edge-count bound 2 (1 - 1/omega) |E| requires, and none of the DNN or Caro–Wei material is reused.",
